We had to keep seeing other teds, even though we knew it's so shitty.
我们不得不继续看其他的 teds，尽管我们知道它很糟糕。

00:47:08.179 --> 00:47:14.900
I feel bad because we knew we had you and then other people come in and nobody could be you.
我感觉很糟糕，因为我们知道我们拥有你，然后其他人进来，没有人可以成为你。

00:47:14.900 --> 00:47:30.940
Great actors, great people came in and you need to go into the studio with a few in the network to test to go into a room with the executives and have you, and as it turned out, Kobe, do chemistry reads and see, we had to have that happen with a couple of other people, but we knew we were in love with you.
伟大的演员、伟大的人进来了，你需要和网络中的一些人一起进入演播室，测试与高管一起进入一个房间并拥有你，结果是，科比，做化学阅读，看看，我们必须和其他几个人一起发生这种情况，但我们知道我们爱上了你。

00:47:30.940 --> 00:47:37.539
All of us were, and that's harrowing because we could have been, we could have had a different feeling than the network.
我们所有人都是如此，这令人痛苦，因为我们本来可以，我们可以有与网络不同的感觉。

00:47:37.539 --> 00:47:46.420
The network would have been like, no, it's not him, and that would have been so heartbreaking, but everybody you went after the other went, we get it, and that doesn't always happen, either, kids.
网络会说，不，这不是他，那会让人心碎，但你追随另一个人的每个人都走了，我们明白了，这也不总是发生，孩子们。

00:47:46.420 --> 00:47:47.659
That does not always happen.
这种情况并不总是发生。

00:47:47.659 --> 00:47:48.659
Yeah.
是的。

00:47:48.659 --> 00:48:03.739
I found in show business, and maybe it's like this in other areas of life, but if a job is not yours, the door won't open, and it just simply won't open, no matter how right you think you are for it, how much you want it.
我在演艺界发现，也许生活的其他领域也是如此，但如果一份工作不是你的，那扇门就不会打开，而且根本就不会打开，无论你认为自己多么适合它，无论你多么想要它。

00:48:03.739 --> 00:48:07.099
If the job is yours, the door's keep flying open.
如果这份工作是你的，那么大门就会一直敞开。

00:48:07.099 --> 00:48:28.500
And I've learned to trust effortlessness in my career, like when you click with people and it's easy and fun, and you're all just the enthusiasm is really high, you want to make this thing, it's like, I don't, I sometimes think effort, like hard grinding effort can be a little overrated, that you need to pay attention to where things are actually in flow.
我学会了在我的职业生涯中相信毫不费力，就像当你与人打交道时，这很容易、很有趣，而且你们都热情很高，你们想要做这件事，就像，我不，我有时认为努力，比如艰苦的努力可能有点被高估了，你需要注意事情实际上在流动的地方。

00:48:28.500 --> 00:48:29.500
Yeah.
是的。

00:48:29.500 --> 00:48:31.500
I've been running this while.
这段时间我一直在跑步。

00:48:31.500 --> 00:48:46.539
And that's cool to hear you say that because I, you know, from the, and you've now been on both sides of the table having, having written and directed your own movies and stuff, like it is, like at the beginning of these sections, you get this list, and, you know, And here's who we're seeing today.
听到你这么说真是太酷了，因为我，你知道，从，你现在已经在桌子两边，编写和导演了自己的电影和东西，就像在这些部分的开头一样，你得到了这个列表，而且，你知道，这就是我们今天看到的人。

00:48:46.539 --> 00:48:50.619
And it's like a list and it's like a name and then a little space for you to write your comments.
它就像一个列表，就像一个名字，然后是一个供您写评论的小空间。

00:48:50.619 --> 00:48:54.219
And so it's just like a very clean sheet of paper with like nine names.
所以它就像一张非常干净的纸，上面有九个名字。

00:48:54.219 --> 00:49:06.920
And you just like see that, you think like these are like nine people right now just hoping that that they're like, and it's by the way, it's this like nine different branches of like where the universe could go.
你就像看到这一点，你认为这些就像现在的九个人，只是希望他们就像，顺便说一句，这就像宇宙可以去的九个不同的分支。

00:49:06.920 --> 00:49:23.440
This could be a show with this person as Ted, this person as Ted, and it's, it's, and I I feel like it's a lot of the stuff we talked about on how I'm in your mother because just the fact that destiny takes such a big part in the search for love.
这可能是一个节目，这个人是泰德，这个人是泰德，我觉得这是我们谈论的很多关于我在你母亲身上的样子，因为命运在寻找爱的过程中扮演了如此重要的角色。

00:49:24.880 --> 00:49:33.599
I feel like how I'm in your mother at its core is this struggle between is falling in love something that I go out and seek.
我觉得我在你母亲身上的核心是这种挣扎，就是坠入爱河和我出去寻找的东西之间。

00:49:33.599 --> 00:49:37.679
Do I take action to meet the person that I spend the rest of my life with?
我是否会采取行动去见那个与我共度余生的人？

00:49:37.679 --> 00:49:39.079
Or is it something that happens to me?
或者是发生在我身上的事情？

00:49:39.079 --> 00:49:40.519
And I have to just sit back and let it happen.
我必须坐下来让它发生。

00:49:40.519 --> 00:49:42.639
And that's the casting process.
这就是铸造过程。

00:49:42.639 --> 00:49:47.119
I mean, really is like, I feel like there's no way to, well, there's a good, no answer to that.
我的意思是，真的就像，我觉得没有办法，嗯，对此没有一个很好的答案。

00:49:47.119 --> 00:49:48.599
It's an unsolvable question.
这是一个无解的问题。

00:49:48.599 --> 00:49:55.920
There's a good, a good theme has emerged of our conversation of just like, there's some preparation and then there's some luck in letting you and being into that part too.
我们的谈话出现了一个很好的主题，就像，有一些准备，然后有一些运气让你也参与到那部分。

00:49:55.920 --> 00:49:57.119
And you're right, Josh, and writing too.
乔什，你是对的，写作也是对的。

00:49:57.119 --> 00:50:01.519
It's like, you can't, if you're forcing it too hard, that might be a sign, it's not quite right.
就像，你不能，如果你强迫得太用力，这可能是一个迹象，这不太正确。

00:50:01.519 --> 00:50:03.559
And the doors did keep opening for you.
大门确实一直为你敞开。

00:50:03.559 --> 00:50:10.820
In some ways, you guys had to honor the themes of your show in the creation of your show.
在某些方面，你们在创作节目时必须尊重节目的主题。

00:50:10.820 --> 00:50:11.659
Yeah.
是的。

00:50:11.659 --> 00:50:12.659
You know what I'm saying?
