When people become so important and kind of iconic in your life, there's that moment when you see them for the first time that kind of gets etched in in your own personal history.
当人们在你的生活中变得如此重要和具有标志性时，你第一次见到他们的那一刻就会铭刻在你自己的个人历史中。

00:52:19.287 --> 00:52:22.399
I'm just curious how you envisioned Robin Sherbotsky.
我只是好奇你是如何想象罗宾·谢尔博茨基的。

00:52:22.399 --> 00:52:25.921
I don't know if that was her last name in the pilot, was it?
我不知道这是否是她在飞行员中的姓氏，是吗？

00:52:25.921 --> 00:52:47.112
I think you came up with Yeah, it's, it was, it was a, it's your Robin, uh, kiddie Sherbotsky is a character from Anna Karenina, I think, I, like, I, I think I was like, I thought I was fainting myself a reader and I was like, I'm gonna read Anna Karenina and, and got like 20 pages into it and then you got what you need, you got what you need and that was it.
我想你想出了是的，这是，这是，这是，这是你的罗宾，呃，小孩子谢尔博茨基是《安娜·卡列尼娜》中的一个角色，我想，我，就像，我，我想我就像，我以为我自己是一个读者，我想，我要读《安娜·卡列尼娜》，然后读了大约20页，然后你得到了你需要的，你得到了你需要的，就是这样。

00:52:46.079 --> 00:52:47.079
Yeah, exactly.
是的，完全正确。

00:52:47.079 --> 00:52:50.760
So you, you, Tolstoy, I gotcha.
所以你，你，托尔斯泰，我明白了。

00:52:50.760 --> 00:52:55.250
Did you have an idea in your head of who this woman was?
你心里知道这个女人是谁吗？

00:52:55.250 --> 00:53:02.331
it's interesting because you've got five main characters, four of them were absolutely drawn from real life.
这很有趣，因为你有五个主要角色，其中四个绝对来自现实生活。

00:53:02.331 --> 00:53:08.036
Like Ted, Marshall and Lily were me, Craig and Rebecca, you know, and again, like then.
就像特德一样，马歇尔和莉莉就是我，克雷格和丽贝卡，你知道，再一次，就像那时一样。

00:53:08.036 --> 00:53:14.987
Then it becomes another writers come in and like add their own hang their own stuff on the Christmas tree.
然后就变成了另一个作家进来，喜欢添加自己的东西，把自己的东西挂在圣诞树上。

00:53:14.987 --> 00:53:29.610
But and Barney was very much inspired by a couple guys that sort of were that that kind of false staffian presence in our lives when we lived in New York, the only character who was completely made up whole cloth was Robin.
但是，巴尼受到了几个家伙的启发，当我们住在纽约时，我们生活中的那种假职员的存在，唯一完全由整块布组成的角色是罗宾。

00:53:29.610 --> 00:53:37.449
And so it really was like the casting process was sort of this process of like, let's see if we can find her.
所以选角过程真的就像是这样的过程，让我们看看是否能找到她。

00:53:37.449 --> 00:53:38.730
Let's see who this could be.
让我们看看这可能是谁。

00:53:38.730 --> 00:53:54.898
It really was like, it wasn't like, oh yeah, that, I mean, having those like, I think Neil got cast as Barney despite the fact that he sort of was physically nothing like the, the people that Barney was was based on, but like that, you know, I remember you guys talking around Jack Black was a prototype.
真的，这不是，哦，是的，我的意思是，有这样的人，我认为尼尔被选为巴尼，尽管事实上他的身体一点也不像巴尼的原型，但就像那样，你知道，我记得你们谈论的杰克·布莱克是一个原型。

00:53:54.898 --> 00:54:05.215
Like, yeah, I think you saw him much more like that was bigger and yeah, yeah, there was there was like a Vince Vaughn road and like a Jack Black road, but we were more down the Jack Black road.
就像，是的，我认为你看到的他更像是更大的，是的，是的，那里有一条像文斯·沃恩的路和一条杰克·布莱克的路，但我们更多的是沿着杰克·布莱克的路。

00:54:05.215 --> 00:54:10.640
I think that wouldn't you say Carter and then like, you know, came in, it was like, shit, that's good.
我想你不会说卡特，然后，你知道，进来，就像，妈的，那很好。

00:54:10.640 --> 00:54:11.385
It's too good.
太好了。

00:54:11.385 --> 00:54:26.329
But I do think the one, the one insight that I think we we happened upon that I'm proud of us for happening upon was is this feeling, because of course, you get picked up, and of course the first thing is like, who can we get in it that will help its chances of getting on the air?
但我确实认为，我认为我们偶然发现的一个让我感到自豪的洞察就是这种感觉，因为当然，你会被选中，当然第一件事就是，我们可以让谁加入来帮助它有机会播出？

00:54:26.329 --> 00:54:27.170
Who's famous?
谁有名？

00:54:27.170 --> 00:54:37.570
But there was a feeling, like, I remember thinking, like, so much of Robin is built into this moment where Ted looks across the crowded bar and sees this person.
但有一种感觉，就像，我记得当时想，就像，罗宾的大部分内容都融入到了泰德穿过拥挤的酒吧并看到这个人的那一刻。

00:54:37.570 --> 00:54:40.969
And we see here for the first time as Ted seeing her for the first time.
我们第一次在这里看到泰德第一次见到她。

00:54:40.969 --> 00:54:56.090
And if it's someone that you already have this built-in expectation of, like, oh, I loved her in this, I hate it or in that, like you're already, you're outside of the moment and you're not having that, it's not that that moment of like, there's a mystery here to be solved.
如果你已经对某个人有这种内在的期望，比如，哦，我爱她这个，我讨厌她，或者那个，就像你已经那样，你就在那个时刻之外，你没有那个时刻，那不是那个时刻，这里有一个谜团需要解决。

00:54:56.090 --> 00:55:02.090
I mean, I want to get to know this person, but I can't be like, you see, you see a person and you're like, I know what you did last summer.
我的意思是，我想了解这个人，但我不能说，你看，你看到一个人，然后你就说，我知道你去年夏天做了什么。

00:55:02.090 --> 00:55:03.090
I can't be.
我不可能。

00:55:03.090 --> 00:55:04.090
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:04.090 --> 00:55:07.050
It has to be like, I have to know what they did last summer.
就像，我必须知道他们去年夏天做了什么。

00:55:07.050 --> 00:55:11.010
You have to not know what they did any summer, because tell me about your summer.
你不必知道他们每个夏天都做了什么，因为请告诉我你的夏天。

00:55:11.010 --> 00:55:17.215
I think a mystery about me and Kobe's relative obscurity or anonymity at that point really served us.
我认为关于我和科比当时相对默默无闻或匿名的神秘感确实对我们很有帮助。

00:55:17.215 --> 00:55:22.130
It served you guys in the story because you're, you're discovering these people.
它对故事中的你们很有帮助，因为你们正在发现这些人。

00:55:22.130 --> 00:55:23.477
You're discovering them.
你正在发现他们。

00:55:23.477 --> 00:55:30.776
And you want to feel like you, you've just happened upon them rather than having any, you know, sort of foreign knowledge of them.
你想要感觉自己只是偶然发现了它们，而不是对它们有任何外国知识。

00:55:30.776 --> 00:55:36.110
Yeah, we, it was perfect who was more famous and who was not more famous in that of those five.
是的，我们，这五个人中，谁更有名，谁不更有名，那就完美了。

00:55:36.110 --> 00:55:37.289
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思？

00:55:37.289 --> 00:55:41.452
like the perfect, the famous people fell into the right spots in the cast.
就像完美的一样，名人在演员阵容中处于正确的位置。

00:55:41.452 --> 00:55:42.858
And, and, and we met you.
还有，还有，我们遇见了你。

00:55:42.858 --> 00:55:44.771
It's the word met is in the title.
标题中就是“遇见”这个词。

00:55:44.771 --> 00:55:46.233
It's about meeting people.
这是关于与人见面。

00:55:46.233 --> 00:55:46.908
We meet Ted.
我们见到了特德。

00:55:46.908 --> 00:55:49.046
We never, we've never seen you before.
我们从来没有见过你。

00:55:49.046 --> 00:55:49.833
We meet Robin.
我们遇见了罗宾。

00:55:49.833 --> 00:55:51.071
And that you're right.
你是对的。

00:55:51.071 --> 00:55:53.208
It was like the audience met you guys.
就像观众认识了你们一样。

00:55:53.208 --> 00:56:03.108
But Carter, it also occurs to me when you're, when you're talking about Robin being invented out of whole cloth on some level, she was the woman you were hoping to meet, right?
但是卡特，当你谈论罗宾在某种程度上被完全创造出来时，我也想到了，她就是你希望见到的女人，对吗？

00:56:03.108 --> 00:56:07.833
Like, she was, you know, she became dimensional and, and spiky and all these things.
就像，她，你知道，她变得立体，尖刺等等。

00:56:07.833 --> 00:56:12.389
But she was is like, what if I looked across the bar and just spotted this woman?
但她说，如果我朝酒吧另一边看到这个女人怎么办？

00:56:12.389 --> 00:56:13.389
What would she be?
她会是什么样子？

00:56:13.389 --> 00:56:14.389
For sure.
一定。

00:56:14.389 --> 00:57:04.737
She was built that way, but it was a combination of, like, make her everything that would be like, of course, he falls in love with this person, but also give her things that it was almost like, you know, it's in sort of like judoing the, like, what's the tension of this series going to be like we've got this character this who just wants to you know his drive is fallen love he's like has this like he gets hit by lightning in this first episode of like ureka I want to get married I'm like ready okay my friend just got engaged I want to I want to settle down like how do we create tension and I feel like that sort of like naturally led to robin just becoming this character that her central drive at least at the beginning is I don't want to settle of that.
她就是这样构建的，但它是一个组合，比如，让她拥有一切，当然，他爱上了这个人，但也给了她一些东西，就像柔道一样，就像，这个系列的张力会是什么样子，就像我们有这个角色，这个角色只是想让你知道他的动力是坠入爱河，他就像在第一集中被闪电击中一样，就像我想要的乌里卡一样结婚了，我准备好了，好吧，我的朋友刚刚订婚，我想要，我想要安定下来，就像我们如何制造紧张一样，我觉得这种感觉自然会导致罗宾成为这个角色，她的中心动力至少在开始时是我不想安定下来。

00:57:04.737 --> 00:57:10.940
But I do remember my first seeing Kobe for the first time, down a hallway, walking towards me.
但我确实记得我第一次见到科比，是在走廊里，向我走来。

00:57:10.940 --> 00:57:15.163
And you know, you just have to do all this, you know, chit chat.
你知道，你只需要做这一切，你知道，闲聊。

00:57:15.163 --> 00:57:19.716
And then you are supposed to, you know, simulate this thing together.
然后你们应该一起模拟这个东西。

00:57:19.716 --> 00:57:22.817
But I do remember at, I think the network test.
但我确实记得，我认为是网络测试。

00:57:22.817 --> 00:57:28.294
So it was just me by the time I think you, you, you just brought me to the network.
所以当我想到你，你，你刚刚把我带到网络时，只有我。

00:57:28.294 --> 00:57:29.218
Is that right?
是这样吗？

00:57:29.218 --> 00:57:30.999
Or did you bring both guys?
还是两个人都带了？

00:57:31.000 --> 00:57:36.701
I feel like in the network you have to still bring two people, I feel like it's always there's always another person.
我觉得在网络里还是得带两个人，我觉得总有另一个人。

00:57:36.701 --> 00:57:37.530
I can't remember.
我不记得了。

00:57:37.530 --> 00:57:43.085
But maybe it was just you at that point because when you were with Kobe in a scene, that was the network, I think.
但也许当时只有你一个人，因为当你和科比一起出现在一个场景中时，我想那就是网络。

00:57:43.085 --> 00:57:44.840
And that was probably just you guys.
那可能只是你们。

00:57:44.840 --> 00:57:46.353
Oh, yeah, that was okay.
哦，是的，没关系。

00:57:46.353 --> 00:57:48.498
So maybe the studio is a big deal.
所以也许工作室很重要。

00:57:48.498 --> 00:57:51.904
That's the last step before you were officially hired.
这是您被正式聘用之前的最后一步。

00:57:51.904 --> 00:57:52.404
Yeah.
是的。

00:57:52.404 --> 00:58:07.984
But I do remember I had gotten I kind of would would get these waves of heroic confidence, like the higher stakes it got, I would get like a little more like, I'm going to get this, you know, like it was my, this competitive street came out in me.
但我确实记得我会得到这些英雄般的信心浪潮，就像赌注越高，我会变得更像是，我会得到这个，你知道，就像这是我的一样，这条竞争性的街道在我身上出现了。

00:58:07.800 --> 00:58:16.399
And I would sometimes say things that were like, like just a little like Hutz-Bah-E in a way that was like risky.
有时我会说一些类似 Hutz-Bah-E 的话，但有点冒险。

00:58:16.399 --> 00:58:21.194
But I remember when Kobe, she threw an actual drink in my face.
但我记得科比的时候，她把一杯饮料泼到了我脸上。

00:58:21.194 --> 00:58:22.639
She had some water.
她有一些水。

00:58:22.639 --> 00:58:37.869
and she threw the water in my face and everyone laughed and I, the scene's over at that point and I turned to the brass at CBS in 20th and I said as if this process weren't humiliating enough.
她把水泼到我脸上，每个人都笑了，而我，那场戏就结束了，我转向 20 号哥伦比亚广播公司的高层，我说，好像这个过程还不够羞辱。

00:58:41.070 --> 00:58:56.206
And it got, you know, it got this like really big laugh and I felt like that was good, you know, I just want them to know, I always hated the power imbalance in being an actor and saying, like, please give me this role.
你知道，它得到了很大的笑声，我觉得这很好，你知道，我只是想让他们知道，我一直讨厌作为一名演员的权力不平衡，并说，就像，请给我这个角色。

00:58:56.206 --> 00:59:01.044
And I always wanted them to know, like, I got something going on here.
我一直想让他们知道，我这里发生了一些事情。

00:59:01.044 --> 00:59:02.565
I hope you understand.
我希望你能理解。

00:59:02.565 --> 00:59:10.306
So I just wanted to level it the tiniest bit because it's so, it's so outsized the power when you walk in there.
所以我只是想把它调平一点，因为当你走进那里时，它的力量是如此之大。

00:59:10.306 --> 00:59:21.780
And there are these executives that run But it's heated in like bleacher level, like theater, like teard seating, like it's a little fee, a little play just for that.
还有这些高管，但它就像露天看台一样激烈，就像剧院一样，就像泪流满面的座位，就像它需要一点费用，只是为此而进行的一点表演。

00:59:21.780 --> 00:59:24.420
The whole thing's stage manage to make you nervous.
整个事情的舞台设法让你紧张。

00:59:24.420 --> 00:59:25.420
It's not comfortable.
这不太舒服。

00:59:25.420 --> 00:59:27.219
It's very stressful and it's on purpose.
这是非常有压力的，而且是故意的。

00:59:27.219 --> 00:59:34.059
They want to see that you can rise to like the like really like under the gun and there's pressure in the air in that room.
他们希望看到你能在枪口下表现得像真正的那样，而且那个房间里的空气有压力。

00:59:34.059 --> 00:59:35.820
And Carter and I of course feel like total frauds.
卡特和我当然感觉自己完全是个骗子。

00:59:35.820 --> 00:59:38.179
We're sitting in these bleachers with all these executives.
我们和所有这些高管坐在看台上。

00:59:38.179 --> 00:59:44.360
Meanwhile two months earlier, where the people you know bringing our little script to them, like please you know we were the you a month earlier.
与此同时，两个月前，你认识的人把我们的小剧本带给他们，就像请你知道我们就是一个月前的你。

00:59:44.360 --> 00:59:46.599
And now we're in the judgey seats.
现在我们坐在评委席上。

00:59:46.599 --> 00:59:53.199
And so I felt, I had such empathy for you in that moment, but you were great and human Kobe, the energy of human Kobe, undeniable.
所以我觉得，在那一刻我对你非常同情，但你是伟大的、人性的科比，人性科比的能量，不可否认。

00:59:53.199 --> 01:00:00.159
I did feel loved and supported by you guys, by Pam, by Rob Greenberg, by Megan and Dylan.
我确实感受到了你们、帕姆、罗布·格林伯格、梅根和迪伦的爱和支持。

01:00:00.159 --> 01:00:06.239
Like I felt like the people that I had established this rapport was in that first room were really on my side.
我觉得在第一个房间里与我建立了这种融洽关系的人真的站在我这边。

01:00:06.239 --> 01:00:09.719
So I felt really, I felt some wind at my sales.
所以我真的觉得我的销售有一些风。

01:00:09.719 --> 01:00:19.978
But I remember, I can't remember if you, we got the offer or it might have been a Friday, maybe had to wait till Monday.
但我记得，我不记得你，我们是否收到了录用通知，或者可能是星期五，也许必须等到星期一。

01:00:19.978 --> 01:00:21.431
I can't remember.
我不记得了。

01:00:21.431 --> 01:00:28.527
I think it was, I don't think it was immediate, but I got the job like within days.
我认为是的，我不认为这是立竿见影的，但我几天之内就得到了这份工作。

01:00:28.527 --> 01:00:33.570
And then next, you know, we're making a podcast about this.
接下来，你知道，我们正在制作一个关于此的播客。

01:00:33.570 --> 01:00:44.000
Do you guys know the West Memphis three, the three kids who were railroaded into, they were on death row for killing this.
你们知道西孟菲斯三人组吗？这三个孩子被火车撞进，他们因为杀人而被关进死牢。

01:00:44.000 --> 01:00:48.360
I think girl, it was kind of a satanic panic thing.
我认为女孩，这有点像撒旦的恐慌。

01:00:48.360 --> 01:00:53.679
And they were called the West Memphis 3 and they got put on death row as teenagers.
他们被称为西孟菲斯三人组，十几岁时就被关进死牢。

01:00:53.679 --> 01:00:56.889
And they were, they were totally innocent.
他们是，他们完全无辜。

01:00:56.889 --> 01:00:58.630
It was like an absolute sham.
这绝对是一场骗局。

01:00:58.630 --> 01:01:01.389
But I think they were on death row for about 20 years.
但我认为他们在死囚牢房里待了大约20年。

01:01:01.389 --> 01:01:07.349
And there was this guy, Damien Eccles, who I ended up doing in the evening at Joe's pub with this kind of evening of written letters.
还有一个人，达米安·埃克尔斯（Damien Eccles），我晚上在乔的酒吧里和他一起写了这样的一封信。

01:01:07.349 --> 01:01:19.194
And I met him backstage and he had been on death row for 20 years and I introduced myself to him because I had just seen a documentary about them and he said, I hope it's okay to say that I'm such a fan.
我在后台遇见了他，他已经在死囚牢房里呆了 20 年了，我向他做了自我介绍，因为我刚刚看了一部关于他们的纪录片，他说，我希望可以说我是他们的粉丝。

01:01:19.194 --> 01:01:22.869
I watched so much how I met your mother when I was behind bars.
当我入狱时，我看了很多我是如何遇见你母亲的。

01:01:22.869 --> 01:01:23.551
Oh my God.
我的天啊。

01:01:23.551 --> 01:01:24.301
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

01:01:24.301 --> 01:01:26.415
I've never heard that from him.
我从来没有听他说过这样的话。

01:01:26.415 --> 01:01:30.439
And I said, can I ask you like, what was it about the show?
我说，我能问你一下，这个节目是关于什么的吗？

01:01:30.439 --> 01:01:31.939
I'm always so curious.
我总是那么好奇。

01:01:31.939 --> 01:01:35.689
What was it about the show that that you wanted to see?
您想看的节目是什么？

01:01:35.689 --> 01:01:41.008
And he said, he said it was fake enough that it took me away from where I was.
他说，他说这太假了，它让我离开了原来的地方。

01:01:41.008 --> 01:01:47.077
But it was real enough that it promised a world that I was hoping I could rejoin one day.
但它足够真实，它承诺了一个我希望有一天能重新加入的世界。

01:01:47.077 --> 01:01:47.577
Wow.
哇。

01:01:48.230 --> 01:01:48.730
Wow.
哇。

01:01:48.730 --> 01:01:49.659
That's amazing.
太棒了。

